1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,960
[♪♪]

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,280
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,439
[SNORTS]

4
00:00:05,439 --> 00:00:07,239
This is my little brother
George.

5
00:00:07,239 --> 00:00:09,360
[SNORTS]
This is Mommy Pig.

6
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,600
[SNORTS]

7
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,760
And this is Daddy Pig.

8
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,280
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

9
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,920
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

10
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,080
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:23,119
[HORN HONKING]

12
00:00:23,119 --> 00:00:24,880
NARRATOR:
Mr. Zebra the Postman

13
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,639
is delivering a letter
to Peppa's house.

14
00:00:30,639 --> 00:00:33,040
Zoë Zebra is with
her daddy today.

15
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,320
She has her own letters
to deliver.

16
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:40,680
Hmm. Danny Dog, Suzy Sheep,
Rebecca Rabbit.

17
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:43,400
Ah, Peppa and George.

18
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:47,000
Just these ones left.

19
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,400
Good.
Let's get them delivered.

20
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,919
ZOE:
Yes, Daddy.

21
00:00:51,919 --> 00:00:54,320
Post!
[BOTH GIGGLE]

22
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:57,279
Peppa and George love it
when the post arrives.

23
00:00:57,279 --> 00:00:59,160
We've got two letters.

24
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,239
This one's for Daddy Pig.

25
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:03,879
How exciting.

26
00:01:03,879 --> 00:01:07,560
"Dear Mr. Pig,
please pay your telephone bill."

27
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,759
Oh.

28
00:01:08,759 --> 00:01:10,440
What's a bill?

29
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:13,080
It sounds very boring.

30
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:15,960
[LAUGHS]
Bills are very boring.

31
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,679
Mommy, is the other letter
for you?

32
00:01:18,679 --> 00:01:22,479
No. This one's for
"Peppa and George."

33
00:01:22,479 --> 00:01:23,759
Wow!

34
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:25,839
A letter for George and me.

35
00:01:25,839 --> 00:01:28,399
"Please come
to my birthday party.

36
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:30,200
Love, Zoë Zebra."

37
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,440
Zoë Zebra has invited
Peppa and George

38
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,640
to her birthday party.

39
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,920
Yippee!

40
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,039
[BOTH GIGGLE]

41
00:01:36,039 --> 00:01:37,920
You need to write a reply
to Zoë,

42
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,039
to tell her you are coming
to her party.

43
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:42,520
Can you help us write it,
Mommy?

44
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,720
Of course.

45
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:47,479
Peppa and George are writing
a reply to Zoë.

46
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:49,720
[SNORTS]
What would you like to say?

47
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:51,280
Dear Zoë.

48
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,600
Dear Zoë...

49
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,640
Um... I don't know what
to say next.

50
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:59,119
How about, "We would love
to come to your party.

51
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:01,640
Kind regards,
Peppa and George."

52
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,800
[BOTH GIGGLE]

53
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,800
What color envelope
shall we use?

54
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:08,239
The red one.

55
00:02:08,239 --> 00:02:10,320
Miss Zoë Zebra.

56
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,799
DADDY PIG:
And, last of all, the stamp.

57
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,760
[GIGGLING]

58
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,760
The letter is ready
to be posted.

59
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,880
This is the post box.

60
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:24,079
Here are Danny, Suzy, Pedro,
Rebecca, and Emily Elephant.

61
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:26,799
[MEOWS] 
They are all posting letters.

62
00:02:26,799 --> 00:02:28,200
[ALL LAUGHING]

63
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,760
And here is Peppa,
with her letter.

64
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,000
There.

65
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,280
Now what happens?

66
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,239
[HORN HONKING]

67
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:36,880
Hello, everyone.

68
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:38,120
Hello, Peppa.

69
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,760
Did you get my letter
about my party?

70
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:43,880
Yes. And I've written you
a reply.

71
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,239
Oh, goody.

72
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:49,160
My goodness.
So many letters today.

73
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,440
And this letter is mine.

74
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:54,480
It is very,
very, important.

75
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,000
Is it for me?

76
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,200
Can I open it now?

77
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,040
It is for you, Zoë.

78
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,560
But it must be delivered
before you can open it.

79
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,320
That's how post works.

80
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,560
Oh.

81
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,400
And with so many letters
to deliver today,

82
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,000
I'd better make a start.

83
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,519
Can George and I
come along too?

84
00:03:11,519 --> 00:03:15,079
Hop aboard, Peppa and George.
See you later.

85
00:03:15,079 --> 00:03:18,840
Peppa and George are helping
Mr. Zebra deliver the post.

86
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:21,040
[♪♪]

87
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:23,560
This is Zoë Zebra's house.

88
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:27,799
This letter is addressed
to Miss Zoë Zebra.

89
00:03:27,799 --> 00:03:29,920
Miss Zoë Zebra.

90
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,760
Zoë Zebra.

91
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:34,480
Zoë Zebra.

92
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,640
Zoë Zebra.

93
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:39,040
Oh! All the post
is for Zoë.

94
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,640
That's my letter.

95
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,040
Can I post it?

96
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,280
Certainly.

97
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:44,679
[GIGGLES]

98
00:03:44,679 --> 00:03:46,480
Peppa loves posting letters.

99
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,600
Mommy, look.

100
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,799
All these letters
are for me.

101
00:03:51,799 --> 00:03:53,399
Oh, amazing.

102
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:55,359
Can you read it,
Mommy?

103
00:03:55,359 --> 00:03:59,119
"Dear Zoë, I would love
to come to your party.

104
00:03:59,119 --> 00:04:00,839
From, Danny Dog.

105
00:04:00,839 --> 00:04:03,480
Suzy Sheep's coming
to your party too.

106
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:06,880
And Rebecca, Pedro,
Emily, Candy.

107
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,239
They're all coming
to your party.

108
00:04:09,239 --> 00:04:12,280
[SNORTS]
And this letter is from me.

109
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:15,440
It says, "We are coming
to your party.

110
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:17,479
Love and kisses,
Peppa and George."

111
00:04:17,479 --> 00:04:18,760
[GIGGLES]

112
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,200
[DOORBELL RINGS]

113
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:24,000
Everyone has arrived
for Zoë's party.

114
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,400
ALL:
Happy birthday, Zoë!

115
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,599
Wow.

116
00:04:27,599 --> 00:04:29,599
So many presents.

117
00:04:29,599 --> 00:04:32,640
You'll be writing lots
of thank you letters, Zoë.

118
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,800
[SIGHS]

119
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,719
And who's going to deliver

120
00:04:35,719 --> 00:04:37,800
all those
thank-you letters?

121
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,520
You are, Daddy.

122
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,719
[LAUGHS]

123
00:04:40,719 --> 00:04:42,400
But I can help.

124
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,479
[ALL LAUGHING]

125
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,400
[♪♪]

126
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,719
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

127
00:04:50,719 --> 00:04:52,599
NARRATOR:
It is early morning.

128
00:04:52,599 --> 00:04:54,919
Mommy and Daddy Pig
are still asleep.

129
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:56,880
[SNORING]

130
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,159
[BOTH GIGGLING]

131
00:04:58,159 --> 00:05:00,800
Wakey, wakey,
Mommy and Daddy!

132
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,080
[GRUNTS]

133
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,320
What?

134
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,520
It's time to get up.

135
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,680
It's much too early.

136
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,800
Don't you know
what time it is, Peppa?

137
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,000
No, Daddy.

138
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,039
Our clock doesn't work.

139
00:05:12,039 --> 00:05:14,880
Oh, dear.
Let's see if we can mend it.

140
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,840
[♪♪]

141
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,080
Ah.

142
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,400
The old cuckoo clock.

143
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,360
Why is it called
a cuckoo clock?

144
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,599
[SNORTS]
There's a little wooden bird

145
00:05:24,599 --> 00:05:26,640
inside called a cuckoo.

146
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,560
I've never seen
the cuckoo.

147
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:32,200
That's because we stopped
winding it a long time ago.

148
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,039
The cuckoo got a bit
annoying.

149
00:05:34,039 --> 00:05:37,080
Oh. Can we wind it up again,
please?

150
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,240
[SNORTS]
All right.

151
00:05:40,599 --> 00:05:42,919
Daddy Pig's winding up
the cuckoo clock.

152
00:05:42,919 --> 00:05:44,359
There.

153
00:05:44,359 --> 00:05:47,159
Daddy Pig sets the clock
to the right time.

154
00:05:47,159 --> 00:05:49,520
It is nearly 9:00.

155
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,520
Daddy, can we see
the cuckoo now?

156
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,760
[SNORTS]

157
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,719
You'll see the cuckoo soon.

158
00:05:54,719 --> 00:05:57,120
What does she look like,
Daddy?

159
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,760
Now let me think.

160
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:01,800
She moves her head
like this:

161
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,039
[BOTH LAUGH]

162
00:06:03,039 --> 00:06:05,000
[SNORTS]
And she flaps her wings

163
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,359
like this:

164
00:06:06,359 --> 00:06:07,640
[BOTH LAUGHING]

165
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:11,680
And she says, ahem,
"Cuckoo!"

166
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,320
[BOTH LAUGHING]

167
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,919
[SNORTS THEN CUCKOOS]

168
00:06:14,919 --> 00:06:16,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

169
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:19,479
What a noisy little cuckoo
you are, George.

170
00:06:19,479 --> 00:06:21,560
[CUCKOOS THEN GIGGLES]

171
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,560
[RATTLING]
Look!

172
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,919
It's going to do
something.

173
00:06:25,919 --> 00:06:28,760
[CUCKOOING]

174
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,200
Wow.

175
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:33,039
[GIGGLING]

176
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:34,320
Silly George.

177
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:36,039
You missed the cuckoo.

178
00:06:36,039 --> 00:06:37,760
[CRYING]

179
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,599
The cuckoo was really,
really brilliant.

180
00:06:40,599 --> 00:06:43,200
She went, "Cuckoo!"

181
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,840
And you missed it.

182
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,520
[CRYING]

183
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:48,320
Never mind, George.

184
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,440
You can see cuckoo
next time.

185
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,840
But you'll have to wait.

186
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:55,120
Cuckoo only comes out
once an hour.

187
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,320
Waiting is boring.

188
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:00,280
Come on, George,
let's play outside.

189
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,840
George does not want
to play outside.

190
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:05,080
He is waiting
to see cuckoo.

191
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,680
[TICKING]

192
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,680
It is nearly 10:00.

193
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,680
George has been waiting
for cuckoo for almost an hour.

194
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,159
George, come and play.

195
00:07:14,159 --> 00:07:17,560
Mr., Dinosaur wants you
to play too.

196
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:20,159
[GROWLS]

197
00:07:20,159 --> 00:07:22,400
Grr! Dinosaur.

198
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:26,440
[CUCKOOING]

199
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,840
George has missed
cuckoo again.

200
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,680
[CRYING]

201
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,440
Never mind, George.

202
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:34,120
Why don't you play
in the garden?

203
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:37,440
I'll call you
when it's time to see cuckoo.

204
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,159
[BOTH LAUGHING]

205
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,880
To you, George.

206
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,440
[GIGGLES]

207
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,599
[BOTH LAUGH]

208
00:07:43,599 --> 00:07:46,479
[TICKING]
It is nearly 11:00.

209
00:07:46,479 --> 00:07:48,960
Peppa! George!

210
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,599
Time to see cuckoo.

211
00:07:50,599 --> 00:07:54,320
Quick, George.
You can't miss cuckoo again.

212
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:55,640
Oh.

213
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,120
George is running faster

214
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,679
than he has ever run
before.

215
00:07:58,679 --> 00:08:01,479
[RATTLING]
[PANTING]

216
00:08:01,479 --> 00:08:03,679
[CUCKOOING]

217
00:08:03,679 --> 00:08:05,359
[LAUGHING]

218
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:07,840
George, did you see cuckoo?

219
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:10,039
Cuckoo. Cuckoo.
[GIGGLES]

220
00:08:10,039 --> 00:08:11,479
BOTH:
Cuckoo!

221
00:08:11,479 --> 00:08:15,120
Peppa and George
love playing cuckoos.

222
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,280
Cuckoo.

223
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:19,159
[GIGGLES]
Cuckoo.

224
00:08:19,159 --> 00:08:20,400
It is nighttime.

225
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,960
GEORGE:
Cuckoo. Cuckoo.

226
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,719
Peppa and George
are very sleepy.

227
00:08:24,719 --> 00:08:25,960
Cuckoo.

228
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,239
[YAWNS]

229
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,080
Peppa and George are asleep.

230
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:32,439
[RATTLING]

231
00:08:32,439 --> 00:08:33,640
[CUCKOOING]

232
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,280
Aah!
Is it morning already?

233
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:39,319
Uh, no. Time to sleep.

234
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:41,919
Cuckoo is not very well.

235
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:45,720
He just needs to sleep,
like you and George.

236
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,880
Good night.

237
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,680
Good night,
my little piggies.

238
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:53,920
George, I know
how to make Cuckoo better.

239
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,480
[SNORTS]
We'll wind him up

240
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,720
like Daddy did.

241
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,959
[RATTLING]
[GIGGLING]

242
00:08:58,959 --> 00:09:01,199
Mommy and Daddy
are fast asleep.

243
00:09:01,199 --> 00:09:02,400
[BED SPRINGS CREAKING]

244
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,920
What?
Mommy.

245
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:07,280
Daddy. We've got something
to show you.

246
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:09,840
We've made cuckoo better.

247
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,480
[CUCKOOING]
[SHRIEK]

248
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,560
[ALL LAUGHING]

249
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,920
[SNORTS]

250
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,800
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

251
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,240
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family
are going ice skating today.

252
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,120
[SNORTS]
This will be fun.

253
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,920
Peppa and George have never
been ice skating before.

254
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:35,160
Now, George, you won't be
very good at ice skating,

255
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:36,800
so just do what I do.

256
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:40,680
[LAUGHS]
I'm sure we'll all be very good.

257
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,959
Yes. Especially me.

258
00:09:42,959 --> 00:09:44,760
[BOTH LAUGH]

259
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,680
[SNORTS]
First we need some skates.

260
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:49,920
At the ice rink,
everyone wears skates.

261
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,520
[SNORTS]
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

262
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,160
[SQUEAKS]
Hello, Mommy Pig.

263
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:55,800
We'd like to hire
some skates, please.

264
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,079
There you go.

265
00:09:57,079 --> 00:09:58,319
ALL:
Thank you.

266
00:09:58,319 --> 00:10:00,680
Happy skating.
[BOTH GIGGLE]

267
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:03,480
Here are Suzy Sheep,
Rebecca Rabbit,

268
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:07,120
Danny Dog, Zoë Zebra,
Candy Cat, Emily Elephant,

269
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,520
and Pedro Pony.

270
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:10,079
[ALL LAUGHING]

271
00:10:10,079 --> 00:10:13,040
Peppa's friends can ice-skate
very well.

272
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,280
[NEIGHS]

273
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,680
[SNORTS]

274
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,480
Peppa wants to ice-skate too.

275
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,520
Aah!

276
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,880
Hello, everyone.

277
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:22,199
ALL:
Hello, Peppa!

278
00:10:22,199 --> 00:10:24,280
[BLEATS AND LAUGHS]

279
00:10:25,439 --> 00:10:27,920
Is this your first time
skating?

280
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,400
[SNORTS]
Yes.

281
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,439
Shall I show you
how to skate?

282
00:10:31,439 --> 00:10:36,040
No, thank you, Suzy,
I'm sure I can already do it.

283
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,959
Okay, come on then.

284
00:10:37,959 --> 00:10:39,199
Ooh.

285
00:10:39,199 --> 00:10:40,560
Aah! Ugh.

286
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,680
[ALL LAUGHING]

287
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:44,760
This is impossible.

288
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:48,600
I don't want to do ice-skating
any more.

289
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,319
Don't worry, Peppa,

290
00:10:50,319 --> 00:10:53,120
everyone falls over
when they ice skate.

291
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,000
Even I fall over.

292
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,199
Watch this.
Oopsy daisy.

293
00:10:58,199 --> 00:10:59,439
[LAUGHS]

294
00:10:59,439 --> 00:11:00,760
Silly Daddy.

295
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,120
[BOTH LAUGH]

296
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,560
George would you like
to skate?

297
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,120
No.

298
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:09,040
George has never
ice-skated before

299
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,839
and he is a bit worried. 
I'll look after George

300
00:11:11,839 --> 00:11:14,280
while you teach Peppa
how to skate.

301
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,480
Skating is easy, Peppa.

302
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:21,240
Just push with your feet
and glide.

303
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:24,719
Push, push, glide. See?

304
00:11:24,719 --> 00:11:27,280
Push, push, glide.

305
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:29,360
Push, push, glide.

306
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,839
[GIGGLES]

307
00:11:30,839 --> 00:11:32,280
This is easy.

308
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,560
[SNORTS]
I can do it

309
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,839
on my own now, Mommy.

310
00:11:34,839 --> 00:11:36,040
[GIGGLES]

311
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,439
Push, push, glide.

312
00:11:38,439 --> 00:11:40,520
Push, push, glide.

313
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:42,199
Well done, Peppa.

314
00:11:42,199 --> 00:11:44,240
[GIGGLING AND SNORTING]

315
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:46,760
Look at me! I'm skating!

316
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:47,920
[SNORTS]

317
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:50,040
Peppa is doing
really well.

318
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,920
Yes.
I'm a very good teacher.

319
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,439
[♪♪]

320
00:11:55,439 --> 00:11:57,719
[GIGGLING]

321
00:11:57,719 --> 00:11:59,319
Slow down, Peppa.

322
00:11:59,319 --> 00:12:01,079
You'll bump into someone.

323
00:12:01,079 --> 00:12:05,600
Don't worry, Mommy.
I'm very good at skating.

324
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,680
Oh, where are the brakes?

325
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:10,560
Oh, dear. I forgot
to teach Peppa how to stop.

326
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,760
Oh.

327
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:14,319
Aah! I can't stop!

328
00:12:14,319 --> 00:12:15,560
Look out!

329
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:17,079
ALL:
Whoa!

330
00:12:17,079 --> 00:12:19,360
[ALL LAUGHING]

331
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,520
[SNORTS]

332
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,160
Mommy Pig taught you
to skate,

333
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,000
but I taught you
how to fall over.

334
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,160
Yes.

335
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:27,680
I'm very good
at falling over.

336
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,959
[ALL LAUGHING]

337
00:12:29,959 --> 00:12:31,400
[SNORTS]
George?

338
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,439
Do you want to skate too?

339
00:12:33,439 --> 00:12:34,680
No.

340
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,719
Come on, George.

341
00:12:35,719 --> 00:12:38,280
It's fun.
I'll teach you.

342
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,560
[CLEARS THROAT]

343
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,400
First, you need to...

344
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,640
Whee!

345
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:44,640
George, come back.

346
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,839
I'm teaching you
how to ice-skate.

347
00:12:47,839 --> 00:12:50,360
[GIGGLING]

348
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:53,599
What a surprise.
George can skate beautifully.

349
00:12:53,599 --> 00:12:56,719
Wow! Look at George.

350
00:12:56,719 --> 00:12:58,160
ALL:
Ooh.

351
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:04,520
Very good, George.

352
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,719
[SNORTS]

353
00:13:05,719 --> 00:13:09,640
Now you need to learn
how to stop.

354
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,360
[COUGHS]
[GIGGLES]

355
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:16,079
Well done, George.
You're fantastic, George.

356
00:13:16,079 --> 00:13:20,839
Yes. You did very well,
George, for your first lesson.

357
00:13:20,839 --> 00:13:22,360
[BOTH LAUGHING]

358
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,839
[SNORTS]
Come on, let's skate.

359
00:13:24,839 --> 00:13:26,319
ALL:
Yes.

360
00:13:26,319 --> 00:13:28,000
[GIGGLING]

361
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,120
Peppa and George
love ice-skating.

362
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,199
Everyone loves
ice-skating.

363
00:13:32,199 --> 00:13:33,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

364
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,199
[SNORTS]
Mommy and Daddy taught me

365
00:13:36,199 --> 00:13:39,240
how to skate,
but I taught George.

366
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,520
[GIGGLES]

367
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,160
[SNORTS THEN LAUGHS]

368
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:45,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

369
00:13:50,319 --> 00:13:54,079
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

370
00:13:54,079 --> 00:13:57,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are playing
in the garden.

371
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,760
Oh.

372
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,920
The grass has not been cut
for a while.

373
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,280
It has grown very long.

374
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,480
Come on, George.

375
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,360
[GEORGE GIGGLING
AND SNORTING]

376
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:08,360
PEPPA:
George, where are you?

377
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:10,839
[SNORTS]
I can't see you.

378
00:14:10,839 --> 00:14:12,079
[SNORTS]

379
00:14:12,079 --> 00:14:13,199
[GIGGLES]

380
00:14:13,199 --> 00:14:16,240
George,
I'm coming to get you.

381
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,319
[GEORGE GIGGLING]

382
00:14:18,319 --> 00:14:20,520
Peppa and George cannot
see each other.

383
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,240
[BOTH GIGGLING]

384
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,920
[BOTH LAUGH]

385
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:28,439
Peppa and George love playing
in the long grass.

386
00:14:30,079 --> 00:14:32,520
Daddy Pig is going to read
his newspaper.

387
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:36,920
Ah, what a nice day
for doing nothing.

388
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,120
Daddy Pig loves
doing nothing.

389
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,800
Oh, goodness me,
Daddy Pig.

390
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:43,280
We've let the garden
get a bit out of control.

391
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,719
[SNORTS]
What do you mean, Mommy Pig?

392
00:14:45,719 --> 00:14:46,959
The grass.

393
00:14:46,959 --> 00:14:48,479
It needs cutting.

394
00:14:48,479 --> 00:14:50,400
DADDY PIG:
Oh, I quite like it.

395
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:53,000
It's the wild garden look.

396
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,319
[GIGGLING]

397
00:14:54,319 --> 00:14:57,560
Mommy, Daddy, come and play
in the long grass.

398
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,839
[SNORTS]
It's fun.

399
00:14:58,839 --> 00:15:00,199
[LAUGHS]
Okay.

400
00:15:00,199 --> 00:15:02,599
Let's all play
with this spotty ball.

401
00:15:02,599 --> 00:15:04,719
[BOTH LAUGHING]

402
00:15:06,479 --> 00:15:07,599
Oh.

403
00:15:07,599 --> 00:15:09,400
[SNORTS]
Where's it gone?

404
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,560
The ball is lost
in the long grass.

405
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:14,079
Now we'll never find it.

406
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:17,800
Hmm. Maybe it is time
to cut the grass.

407
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,240
Yes, Daddy Pig.

408
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:22,079
[SNORTS]
I'll get the lawn mower.

409
00:15:22,079 --> 00:15:24,160
I'm sure it's here
somewhere.

410
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,640
[CRASHING AND CLANGING]

411
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,240
Ah! Here it is.

412
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,120
Daddy Pig has found
the lawn mower.

413
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:31,199
[SNORTS]
It's a bit old and rusty.

414
00:15:31,199 --> 00:15:34,640
Nonsense. It'll have the grass
cut in no time.

415
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,160
[CLANGING AND CREAKING]

416
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,400
[GRUNTING]

417
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,640
It does seem a bit rusty.

418
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,680
Maybe I should phone
Grandpa Pig

419
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,920
and ask if we can borrow
his lawnmower.

420
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:46,199
There's no need
to phone Grandpa.

421
00:15:46,199 --> 00:15:49,800
I just need to push
a bit harder. Hmm.

422
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:52,319
Daddy Pig's lawn mower
is not very good.

423
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:53,680
[CREAKING]

424
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:54,880
Oh.

425
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:58,160
I know, let's phone Grandpa.

426
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,880
[RINGING]

427
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,959
Hello, Grandpa Pig
speaking.

428
00:16:03,959 --> 00:16:05,479
Hello, Grandpa Pig.

429
00:16:05,479 --> 00:16:08,400
Could you help us
cut some very long grass?

430
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,880
Oh, ha-ha! Certainly.

431
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,640
I'll be over right away.

432
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,280
Bye.

433
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,599
I think this is a job
for Betsy.

434
00:16:16,599 --> 00:16:18,599
[♪♪]

435
00:16:18,599 --> 00:16:20,359
[HORN HONKS]

436
00:16:20,359 --> 00:16:22,800
Grandpa Pig is driving
his motor mower

437
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,079
over to Peppa's house.

438
00:16:24,079 --> 00:16:26,120
[HORNS HONKING]

439
00:16:30,599 --> 00:16:32,640
[SNORTS]
Grandpa Pig!

440
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:33,839
[SPEAKS GIBBERISH]

441
00:16:33,839 --> 00:16:36,160
[SNORTS]
Hello, everyone.

442
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,920
I hear there's some grass
that needs cutting.

443
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:42,920
And it's just a bit too long
for my lawn mower.

444
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,520
[SNORTS]
Don't worry.

445
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:47,120
Betsy will have it done
in no time.

446
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,959
Is your lawn mower
called Betsy?

447
00:16:49,959 --> 00:16:51,680
She certainly is.

448
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:53,000
[HORN HONKS]

449
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,120
[LAUGHS]
Hello, Betsy.

450
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,520
[HORN HONKS]

451
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,120
[ALL LAUGH]

452
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,839
Grandpa,
can we ride on Betsy?

453
00:17:00,839 --> 00:17:02,400
Of course you can.

454
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:03,599
Hop aboard.

455
00:17:03,599 --> 00:17:05,720
Aye, aye, Captain Grandpa.

456
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,560
[SNORTS]

457
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,639
We'll have this grass
cut in no time.

458
00:17:10,639 --> 00:17:13,040
Hold tight. Here we go.

459
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,720
ALL:
Whee!

460
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,440
[LAUGHS]

461
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,800
[WHIRRING]

462
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,800
Betsy is very good
at cutting grass.

463
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:22,359
[LAUGHS]
This is fun.

464
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:24,480
[GIGGLING]

465
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:28,600
[♪♪]

466
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,919
There. Finished.

467
00:17:31,919 --> 00:17:34,159
Grandpa,
you've missed a bit.

468
00:17:34,159 --> 00:17:37,560
GRANDPA PIG:
Oh, yes.

469
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,879
What's this?

470
00:17:40,879 --> 00:17:42,960
Oh. The spotty ball.

471
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,240
[GIGGLES]

472
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,919
Thank you for finding our ball,
Grandpa.

473
00:17:46,919 --> 00:17:49,159
And thank you
for cutting the grass.

474
00:17:49,159 --> 00:17:52,040
Cutting grass is easy
with Betsy.

475
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,320
[HORN HONKS]

476
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,399
[ALL LAUGHING]

477
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:58,399
[SNORTS]
Now we can play

478
00:17:58,399 --> 00:17:59,680
with our spotty ball.

479
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,919
[GIGGLES]

480
00:18:00,919 --> 00:18:02,960
To you, Daddy.

481
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,680
The ball bounces very well
on the short grass.

482
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:08,440
[CHUCKLES]
To you, George.

483
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,680
[GIGGLING]

484
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:11,080
[SPEAKS GIBBERISH]

485
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,480
[LAUGHS]

486
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,960
Catch.

487
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:16,040
[ALL LAUGHING]

488
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:21,200
[♪♪]

489
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,919
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

490
00:18:22,919 --> 00:18:25,840
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

491
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,560
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

492
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:30,159
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

493
00:18:30,159 --> 00:18:31,840
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

494
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,919
[GIGGLING]

